course: dictionary
lesson: 13941
title: The word lesser
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lesser is an adjective, a describing word. It usually compares two things and means smaller in amount or size, or less important. «Eight is the lesser of 8 and 12.» Eight is smaller, so it is the lesser one.
explain: The opposite of lesser is greater. When you meet lesser, ask yourself: smaller than what? The other thing is usually nearby in the sentence, like «the lesser of two numbers».
explain: Lesser can also mean less important or not as good. «A lesser prize» is a smaller or less valuable prize. «The lesser of two evils» means the less bad choice out of two bad choices. Always check the words around it to find which meaning fits.
fact: Lesser means smaller in amount or size, or less important or not as good.
fact: «The lesser number» is the smaller of two numbers.
fact: «Subtract the lesser number from the greater» gives you the difference between them.
fact: «The lesser of two evils» means the less bad of two bad choices.
fact: Some animal and plant names use lesser for the smaller kind, such as «the lesser spotted woodpecker».
exercise: «Tom has 7 marbles and Ana has 12. Which is the lesser number?» | 12 | *7 | 19
exercise: «The team won a lesser prize than the champions.» What does lesser mean here? | Shiny | Bigger | *Less important or not as valuable | Very loud
exercise: «Which is the lesser number: 45 or 54?» | Both are the same | *45 | 54
test: «Subtract the lesser number from the greater: 9 and 4. What is the difference?» | 9 | 13 | 36 | *5
test: «Picking the bus was the lesser of two evils, since both were late.» What does lesser of two evils mean? | *The less bad of two bad choices | The most dangerous choice | The greatest good | Smaller in size
exam: «The lesser spotted woodpecker is a smaller kind of woodpecker.» In this name, what does lesser mean? | Bigger | Brightest | Less bad | *The smaller kind
